{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## The problem\n\nThe operator has adopted option (a) of bug `f850-674c-c89f-4b97` (`unsuited-locustal-incatern`):\n**Windows IS a declared support target for rebar.** That decision currently lives only in epic\n`55da-cee1-e556-4735` (`simple-brotherly-peacock`) and in the bug's comment trail. It creates\nstanding obligations on all future work under `src/rebar` — no unguarded POSIX-only syscall, no\nPOSIX mode bits as a security property, no locale-default text encoding at an I/O boundary — and\nthose obligations need a citable home in the tree, not only in a ticket.\n\nThe decomposition agent drafted `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md` (155 lines,\nstatus Proposed) plus its `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` marker and a regenerated `README.md`, but left\nthem UNCOMMITTED in a scratch worktree at `/Users/joeoakhart/adr-windows-support-target/`. A\ncleanup of that directory loses the draft. This task recovers and lands it.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Do change:**\n- add `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md`\n- add the `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` reservation marker\n- regenerate `docs/adr/README.md` with `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` — never hand-edit it\n\n**Do NOT change:** `.github/workflows/test.yml` (that is S10,\n`arbitrary-nautical-spreadwing`), `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` or `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py`\n(that is S1, `friendless-alabaster-cub`, in flight), or `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`\n(that is S11).\n\nThis change is additive documentation only. It adds two files and one generated line to an index;\nit runs no migration and mutates no store, so there is nothing to back up and nothing to roll back\nbeyond reverting the commit.\n\n## Second-pair-of-eyes obligation\n\nThe draft is a first draft and must be reviewed against the epic's measured evidence rather than\nadopted as written. Every assertion that cites a line number, a file, a commit, a job duration or a\nfailure count is re-checked against the tree or the cited CI run; any that does not hold is\ncorrected before landing, and the correction is recorded as a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Number re-verification\n\n`0117` is re-verified free at implementation time rather than trusted from the draft: the\n`docs/adr/.numbers/` markers and the `docs/adr/0*.md` files must be in bijection on current\n`origin/main`, with no `0117` marker present, before the marker is added.\n\n## Testing\n\n```\npython scripts/check_adr_numbers.py                                   # markers <-> ADR files bijection\npython scripts/gen_adr_index.py && git diff --exit-code docs/adr/README.md   # index generated, not hand-edited\nuv run --no-sync pytest -k \"adr or docs\" -m \"not integration and not external\" -q -p no:cacheprovider\nmake lint && make typecheck\ngit diff --name-only origin/main                                      # only docs/adr/ paths\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md` exists and states that Windows is a\n      declared support target. Proof: `grep -q \"Windows is a declared support target\"\n      docs/adr/0117-windows-declared-support-target.md`.\n- [ ] Its `**Status:**` line follows the repo convention used by every other landed ADR. Proof:\n      `grep -c \"^\\*\\*Status:\\*\\* Proposed\" docs/adr/0*.md` is unchanged from `origin/main`, checked\n      against the tree rather than assumed.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/.numbers/0117` exists and the markers remain in bijection with the ADR files.\n      Proof: `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/README.md` lists 0117 and is byte-identical to a fresh generator run. Proof:\n      `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py && git diff --exit-code docs/adr/README.md`.\n- [ ] Every line number, file path, commit, job duration and failure count asserted in the ADR has\n      been re-checked against the tree or against run `33824556786`, and each one that did not hold\n      is corrected. Proof: the corrections are enumerated in a comment on this ticket, each naming\n      what was checked and what it actually said.\n- [ ] No file outside `docs/adr/` is touched. Proof: `git diff --name-only origin/main` lists only\n      `docs/adr/` paths.\n- [ ] The repo gates are green. Proof: `make lint` and `make typecheck` both exit 0, with the\n      complexity and mechanism ratchets reporting `new=0 increased=0`.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788575231784605730,"uuid":"ef26b2db-ddb4-4221-bf35-be48eee31e5e"}